# Godmode adapter for Cursor

Copy this file to `.cursor/rules/godmode.mdc` in the target project. Cursor
rules are advisory text, so this host runs Godmode in its most honest mode:
the runtime's own gates stay HARD (they are exit codes, not prose), and
everything host-side is labelled truthfully below.

## Session contract

Open substantive work with `python scripts/godmode.py --project . session open
--label <task>`; close with `session close` and treat a non-zero exit as a
blocker, not advice. Set `GODMODE_HOST=cursor` and `GODMODE_ENFORCEMENT=SOFT`.
Route checks through `verify`, state claims through `claim --cite ...`, gate
mutations behind `planmode`, and preview protected operations with `guard`.

## Enforcement on this host — mixed, reported truthfully

| Control | Level |
| --- | --- |
| attestation_gate | HARD |
| claim_downgrade | HARD |
| plan_mode_mutation_gate | HARD |
| status_reopen_guard | HARD |
| authority_claim_detection | HARD |
| interactive_authorization | SOFT |
| tool_call_interception | UNAVAILABLE |

interactive_authorization is SOFT because auto-run settings can bypass the
confirmation prompt; tool_call_interception is UNAVAILABLE because rules
expose no pre-tool boundary. Claims resting on either stay unverified — say
so rather than rounding up.
